# The corpus signatures are written on Windows and read here, and git was
# showing all sixty lines of a file as changed when one number had moved.
# A diff that says "everything changed" is a diff nobody reads, which is the
# opposite of what a signature is for.
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# Books are archives. Nothing may touch a byte inside them — a corpus whose
# files git has "helpfully" corrected is a corpus measuring the wrong thing.
*.epub binary
*.cbz binary
*.cbr binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
